 "summary": "A CLI tool that extracts text from a PDF and queries Google Gemini for answers. The implementation works but is a single large script with limited safety and missing many advertised features.",
 "strengths": [
  "Clear README with step‑by‑step setup instructions",
  "Prompt includes explicit rules to keep answers grounded in the PDF",
  "Retry logic for transient Gemini API errors"
 ],
 "top_fixes": [
  "Refactor main.py: split PDF loading, prompt building, and API call into separate functions to reduce the 97‑line main function.",
  "Add input validation for the PDF path (existence, size limits) and enforce a hard token limit before sending to the model.",
  "Implement a proper conversation loop that stores and passes chat history, and add a graceful shutdown on 'quit'."
 ],
